world-atlas is built from Natural Earth (https://www.naturalearthdata.com/),
which is released into the public domain. The country outlines embedded in
index.html were decoded from world-atlas TopoJSON, split at the antimeridian,
and simplified to 0.25 degrees for this project.

No other third-party code, fonts, or assets are bundled. The page declares
system font stacks by name and loads no font files. It makes no network
requests at runtime; the only external URLs are citation links the reader
chooses to click.
